Certainly! For my dinner party, I've selected the following historical figures: 

 Albert Einstein, a theoretical physicist whose groundbreaking work on the theory of relativity is unparalleled in the field;
 Mahatma Gandhi, an influential leader for India's independence movement and a renowned figure for his philosophy of pacifism and nonviolence;
 Marie Curie, a pioneering physicist and chemist, best known for her discovery of the radioactive elements radium and polonium, and her work on radioactivity decay;
 Nelson Mandela, political activist who fought against apartheid in South Africa and became the first black President of the country after being released from prison;
 Leonardo da Vinci, Italian polymath who is renowned for his artistic talents as well as his scientific pursuits; 
 Isaac Newton, renowned English mathematician, physicist, and astronomer who laid the groundwork for classical mechanics with his law of universal gravitation;
 Confucius, one of the most important figures in Chinese history and culture, whose philosophical teachings continue to influence the East and West alike.

I am sure this diverse lineup would provide enlightening conversations and enriching company over dinner. 

With these luminaries at the table, I expect our discussions will traverse various topics such as science, art, history, and morality - all subjects where these figures were, in their respective times, trailblazers. It promises to be an unforgettable evening.
